## Issues

- [ ] `description` is 436 chars (cap 200) — packs the consumer-agnostic core,
  the dual entry points, the silent-on-create pattern, the inherent-decision
  pause list (brain root, MCP merge, IDE), and the brain MCP entry derivation.
  Trim to ≤200 chars.
  Traces to: `description` field | Brevity Contract caps
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Brevity

- [ ] `intent` is ~591 words (cap 100). Restates the description with added
  paragraphs about the confirmation-reserved-for-overwrites rule, category
  enumeration, brain layer specifics, MCP server runtime brain tool, sync
  contract, four-state vocabulary. Trim to ≤100 words.
  Traces to: `intent` field | Brevity Contract caps
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Brevity

- [ ] `outcomes.desired` has 10 items (cap 4); each is paragraph length and
  encodes implementation contracts: the InitStep contract shape, the
  planning-vs-apply two-call pattern, the skip-existing protocol, the
  per-category enum membership, prescription pattern for MCP merge, dual
  entry point parity. Compress to 3-4 domain success criteria.
  Traces to: `outcomes.desired` | Brevity Contract caps + Forbidden content (function names, type signatures, exact strings)
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Brevity, Forbidden-content

- [ ] `outcomes.undesired` has ~10 paragraph-length items. Compress to 3-4.
  Traces to: `outcomes.undesired` | Brevity Contract caps
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Brevity

- [ ] `## Context` is ~700 words (cap ~150). Recapitulates cold-start, consumer
  divergence, brain layer architecture, InitStep wizard pattern, prescription
  pattern. Most duplicates trunk and root.
  Traces to: `## Context` | Brevity Contract caps + Sibling-redundancy
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Brevity, Sibling-redundancy

- [ ] `## Strategy` has ~12 paragraph-length decisions (cap ~5 ≤80 words).
  Most encode implementation contracts; move to plan and code.
  Traces to: `## Strategy` | Brevity Contract caps + Forbidden content
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Brevity, Forbidden-content

- [ ] `## Good examples` and `## Bad examples` reproduce full structured-JSON
  responses, full agent dialog blocks, full terminal output. Cap is 2-3
  brief; exact strings forbidden.
  Traces to: examples sections | Forbidden content
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Forbidden-content

- [ ] Sibling redundancy with each child install helper spec (`installAgents`,
  `installMethodologyDocs`, `provisionBrain`, `scaffoldCommands`,
  `scaffoldReadme`, `writeMethodology`, `configureIde`, `initContent`):
  this parent enumerates each child's contract then each child restates it.
  Parent should hold cross-cutting invariants only.
  Traces to: outcomes, Strategy | Sibling-redundancy
  Misalignment: spec-gap
  Category: Sibling-redundancy

- [ ] Carry-forward (prior cycle): "items 1 and 3 from prior pass confirmed
  resolved. One item remains." Re-walk that remaining item against the
  rewritten spec; the item may be subsumed by the prune.

## Retro

The install service spec is the bloat-cascade epicenter — it documents the
contract shape, the consumer parity, AND every category by name. Each child
spec then restates its own slice. The parent should hold cross-cutting
invariants and a brief "categories are: framework, methodology, agents,
commands, skills, MCP, brain, IDE, readme" pointer; the contract details
of each category live with that category.

Recommended sequence: rewrite this spec AFTER the project root and
`src/.aide` are pruned, BEFORE the child install specs, so the child
specs can confidently prune content the parent now owns.
